Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 08:42:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 12/41] grpc: wire BlockStream tonic server into
 init_rpc_servers + GrpcConfig
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 1a step 3 — the streaming server is now actually started when
config.rpc.grpc.enable is true. Release build clean (3:14 from cold).
Default is disabled (opt-in), so this commit is a no-op for any operator
who doesn't explicitly turn it on — bin RPC continues to be the only
exposed surface.

Config (src/config/rpc.rs):
- New GrpcConfig with address / port / enable / public-bind safety guard.
  Same shape as UnrestrictedRpcConfig but standalone (no shared block) —
  gRPC doesn't have the restricted/unrestricted split since the streaming
  endpoint exposes the same blockchain data the unrestricted bin RPC does.
- grpc_rpc_port(): default 18091 mainnet, 28091 testnet, 38091 stagenet —
  follows the +10 pattern from the existing 18081/18089 choice.
- Public-bind guard: panics on non-local address unless
  i_know_what_im_doing_allow_public_grpc is set, mirroring the
  i_know_what_im_doing_allow_public_unrestricted_rpc guard for bin RPC.

Server wire-up (src/rpc/server.rs):
- After the bin RPC spawn loop, an additional tokio task spawns the gRPC
  server when enabled. Uses tonic::transport::Server::builder().add_service.
- Reuses the same blockchain_read / blockchain_context / txpool_read /
  tx_handler clones — the streaming service feeds from the same internal
  state as the bin RPC, so all of cuprate's data-layer optimizations
  (TX-pruning, batch index lookup, BlockHashInRange) apply transparently.
- One eprintln "[GRPC] Starting BlockStream server at <addr>" on boot so
  the operator can see in the log that the streaming endpoint is live;
  the per-stream PERF logs from grpc.rs take over from there.

Next: gRPC client in monero-gui wallet (Phase 1b) — first end-to-end
streaming sync test against this server with grpcurl, then wallet
integration.
